qemu-rdp: relative mouse motion for a guest without an absolute pointer

qemu-rdp passed every pointer position the client sent to QEMU as SetAbsPosition, which QEMU refuses
while the guest's mouse is relative ("Mouse is not absolute"): a PS/2 mouse without a USB tablet (a
Windows 9x VM) or the Sun mouse of a SPARCstation, where only the buttons then arrived.

- While the D-Bus Mouse's IsAbsolute is false, a position goes to QEMU as RelMotion, the difference
  to the client's previous position (the guest's own acceleration applies, as with VNC's relative
  mode).
- A client in relative mouse mode (RelMove) gets RelMotion too, and the middle button is passed on.

For wsh-pve (packages/wsh-qemu-rdp), against qemu-display at the commit upstream.env pins.
---
diff --git a/qemu-rdp/src/server/input.rs b/qemu-rdp/src/server/input.rs
index a38a4d8..85e320c 100644
--- a/qemu-rdp/src/server/input.rs
+++ b/qemu-rdp/src/server/input.rs
@@ -34,6 +34,8 @@ impl RdpServerInputHandler for InputHandler {
 }
 
 async fn input_receive_task(mut rx: Receiver<InputEvent>, console: Console) {
+    // The last position the client sent, for a guest without an absolute pointer
+    let mut last: Option<(u16, u16)> = None;
     loop {
         let res = match rx.recv().await {
             Some(InputEvent::Keyboard(ev)) => match ev {
@@ -52,8 +54,25 @@ async fn input_receive_task(mut rx: Receiver<InputEvent>, console: Console) {
             Some(InputEvent::Mouse(ev)) => match ev {
                 MouseEvent::Move { x, y } => {
                     tracing::trace!(?x, ?y);
-                    console.mouse.set_abs_position(x.into(), y.into()).await
+                    // A guest with only a relative pointer (a PS/2 or Sun mouse, no USB tablet)
+                    // refuses SetAbsPosition: it gets the motion since the last position instead
+                    let previous = last.replace((x, y));
+                    if console.mouse.is_absolute().await.unwrap_or(true) {
+                        console.mouse.set_abs_position(x.into(), y.into()).await
+                    } else if let Some((px, py)) = previous {
+                        let (dx, dy) = (i32::from(x) - i32::from(px), i32::from(y) - i32::from(py));
+                        if dx != 0 || dy != 0 {
+                            console.mouse.rel_motion(dx, dy).await
+                        } else {
+                            Ok(())
+                        }
+                    } else {
+                        Ok(())
+                    }
                 }
+                MouseEvent::RelMove { x, y } => console.mouse.rel_motion(x, y).await,
+                MouseEvent::MiddlePressed => console.mouse.press(MouseButton::Middle).await,
+                MouseEvent::MiddleReleased => console.mouse.release(MouseButton::Middle).await,
                 MouseEvent::RightPressed => console.mouse.press(MouseButton::Right).await,
                 MouseEvent::RightReleased => console.mouse.release(MouseButton::Right).await,
                 MouseEvent::LeftPressed => console.mouse.press(MouseButton::Left).await,
